{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection"],"declarations":50,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.char_difference_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.char_difference_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":594,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L594-L614","doc":"The difference of the two characters vanishes only at `q = 1`. If both legs\nwere γγ-produced their characters would both be `1`, so the difference would be\nexactly `0`; it is not, at any `q > 0` with `q ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.perm_neutronWord_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.perm_neutronWord_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":589,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L589-L592","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.perm_protonWord_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.perm_protonWord_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":581,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L581-L587","doc":"**The headline.** *No re-ordering* of the proton word has character `1`, so\nno ordering of its letters is a γγ-produced word. The γγ ruling picked an\nordering; the invariant cannot see one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.neutronWord_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.neutronWord_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":578,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L578-L579","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.protonWord_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.protonWord_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":573,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L573-L576","doc":"The proton word is **not** a γγ-produced word: its alternating character is\nstrictly negative, and `altChar_eq_one` makes every γγ word's character `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.neutronWord_char_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.neutronWord_char_neg","kind":"theorem","line":567,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L567-L571","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.protonWord_char_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.protonWord_char_neg","kind":"theorem","line":561,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L561-L565","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.both_corpus_budgets_are_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.both_corpus_budgets_are_odd","kind":"theorem","line":551,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L551-L559","doc":"**Neither of the corpus's two crossing budgets is admissible**, and they\nfail for the same reason: `6 + 3 + 2 = 11` and `6 + 3 = 9` are both odd.\n\nStated on the lengths alone, so it is checkable without reference to any\nparticular letters. The point is the one the 9-vs-11 argument keeps missing:\nthose two budgets differ by 2, so no choice between them changes the parity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.even_dressing_cannot_repair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.even_dressing_cannot_repair","kind":"theorem","line":530,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L530-L549","doc":"**An even-length dressing can never repair an inadmissible word.**\n\nThis closes the obvious repair route. Given the result above, the natural move\nis to add structure until the parity comes right — and the structure the ruling\nsupplies is γγ pair-production, whose words are **even** by\n`GammaGammaWordSelection.length_even`. Appending an even-length dressing\npreserves the parity, so it preserves inadmissibility.\n\nSo a nucleon that fails here cannot be fixed by adding γγ vertices, however\nmany. Whatever supplies the missing odd letter is by that very fact **not**\nγγ-produced — which is the same boundary the parity bound already draws around\nthe quark block, arrived at from the other side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gluon_dressing_must_be_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gluon_dressing_must_be_odd","kind":"theorem","line":504,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L504-L528","doc":"**The gluon dressing must have ODD length.**\n\nGiven an even-length core and an odd-length quark block — which is what the\ncorpus construction supplies — the assembled word is admissible in the\nalternating block exactly when the gluon dressing is odd.\n\nThis is the crossing-budget statement *as reading 1 sees it*: it does not name a\nnumber, it fixes a parity, and every gluon count the corpus has proposed (2, and\nthe retracted 4) is even and therefore fails it.\n\n🛑 **It has no force under the live reading 3** (section note above). Measured\nacross every generator assignment and every dressing over the alphabet, reading\n3 admits *every* count `k = 0…3` for both nucleons — 4/8, 18/48, 149/288,\n594/1728 for the proton — so there is no parity signal and no monotone in `k`.\n**Reading 3 does not decide the crossing budget.** Keep this theorem for the\nparked reading, and do not cite it as excluding a corpus gluon count today. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.alt_psd_iff_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.alt_psd_iff_even","kind":"theorem","line":479,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L479-L489","doc":"The companion positive statement, recorded so the exclusion above is not\nmistaken for \"the character is always negative\": at **even** length it is always\npositive, so the parity is a real discriminator rather than a blanket sign.\nTogether with `GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar_eq_one` (every γγ word has\ncharacter `1 > 0`) this is consistent — γγ words have even length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.no_eleven_letter_word_is_alt_psd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.no_eleven_letter_word_is_alt_psd","kind":"theorem","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L460-L477","doc":"**The headline: no 11-letter word can be PSD in the alternating block.**\n\nThe alternating block is one-dimensional, so `Matrix.PosSemidef` there is\nexactly `0 ≤ wordChar`. Eleven is odd, so the character is strictly negative —\nfor every assignment of letters, every ordering, every generator labelling.\n\n🛑 **Under READING 1 only** (see the section note above; reading 3 is the live\none and does not constrain this block). Within reading 1 it is a **scope-(b)\nstructural exclusion** of the entire 11-crossing nucleon construction, with the\ninvariant named: the sign of the alternating character. It is independent of\nwhich letters carry the proton/neutron asymmetry, so no choice among them can\nrepair it — which is why it excludes *every* corpus nucleon model rather than\nselecting among them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_pos_of_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_pos_of_even","kind":"theorem","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L455-L458","doc":"An **even-length** word has strictly positive alternating character. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_neg_of_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_neg_of_odd","kind":"theorem","line":450,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L450-L453","doc":"An **odd-length** word has strictly negative alternating character. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_sign","kind":"theorem","line":424,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L424-L448","doc":"**The sign of a word's alternating character is `(−1)^{length}`.**\n\nStated as the two halves at once, because that is what the induction proves:\nprepending a letter flips both the parity and the sign together. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.letterChar_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.letterChar_neg","kind":"theorem","line":408,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L408-L422","doc":"**Every letter of the alphabet has strictly negative alternating\ncharacter**, at every `q > 0`.\n\nFalsifiable and checked at all three constructors rather than asserted: it is\nthe reason the parity below holds, and it fails the moment a letter with shift\n`d ≥ 1/(q² − 1)` is admitted — none of the corpus letters is remotely near that\n(`d ∈ {0, −1/2, −1}` against a threshold of `≈ 4.31` at the substrate pin). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.ud_mul_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.ud_mul_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L338-L358","doc":"**The obstruction, isolated.** The mixed letter's character multiplies with\n*no* letter of the alphabet — itself included — to give `1`, at any `q > 0`\nother than `q = 1`. Every corpus nucleon word carries exactly two of these\nletters, so no pairing of them can be absorbed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.neutronWord_char","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.neutronWord_char","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L316-L322","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.protonWord_char","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.protonWord_char","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L308-L314","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.core_char","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.core_char","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L301-L306","doc":"**Positive control.** The three-vertex core has character `1`, so the model\ncan see a γγ word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.neutronWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.neutronWord","kind":"def","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L297-L298","doc":"The same for the neutron: quark block `ud ud dd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.protonWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.protonWord","kind":"def","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L293-L295","doc":"`pyhecke.atom.build_atom_nf_exact` for the proton: the core, the `uu ud ud`\nquark block, and the two-letter gluon dressing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.core","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.core","kind":"def","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L290-L291","doc":"`β_Bor = (σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³` as shifted letters: three γγ vertices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.uu_mul_dd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.uu_mul_dd","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L282-L286","doc":"One γγ vertex, as a pair of shifted letters: `(−q⁻¹)(−q) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_of_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_of_perm","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L273-L279","doc":"**Ordering blindness.** The character of a shifted-letter word depends only\non the multiset of its letters — it is a product of scalars, and `R` is\ncommutative. This is the lemma that makes the exclusion below cover every\nordering at once, and so covers whatever ordering the γγ ruling picks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_append","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L268-L270","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar_nil","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L265-L265","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.letterChar_eq_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.letterChar_eq_shift","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L252-L262","doc":"**The three letter characters are `S + d` for the corpus shifts**, with\n`S = −q⁻¹` and `h = q − q⁻¹`. This is the tie to the corpus; without it the\nconstants below would be free-floating. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.wordChar","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L249-L250","doc":"The alternating character of a shifted-letter word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.letterChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.letterChar","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L241-L247","doc":"The alternating character of a single shifted letter. Since the character\nis an algebra hom, `χ(σᵢ + d·1) = χ(σᵢ) + d = −q⁻¹ + d`; `letterChar_eq_shift`\nchecks that these three values are exactly that, for the three corpus shifts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.instReprLetter.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.instReprLetter.repr","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L237-L237","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.instReprLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.instReprLetter","kind":"instance","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L237-L237","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.instDecidableEqLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.instDecidableEqLetter","kind":"instance","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L237-L237","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.Letter.dd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.Letter.dd","kind":"ctor","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L236-L236","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.Letter.ud","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.Letter.ud","kind":"ctor","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L235-L235","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.Letter.uu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.Letter.uu","kind":"ctor","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L234-L234","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.Letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.Letter","kind":"inductive","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L229-L237","doc":"The corpus nucleon alphabet: a letter is `σᵢ + d` with the shift `d` drawn\nfrom `{0, −h/2, −h}`, named after the quark pair it encodes (`uu` a positive\ncrossing, `ud` the mixed pair, `dd` the inverse `σᵢ⁻¹`). The generator index is\ndeliberately absent — `altChar_regen` above is why that loses nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.vertex_one_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.vertex_one_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L222-L225","doc":"Both four-strand vertices really are γγ words, so the index set above is\ninhabited at both values and `gammaGamma_fourStrand_indices` is not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gammaGamma_fourStrand_indices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gammaGamma_fourStrand_indices","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L211-L220","doc":"**Four strands: two vertices, and the collapse stops.** On `H₄` the indices\navailable are `0` and `1`, so a γγ word carries an arbitrary binary list and the\none-integer argument of `gammaGamma_threeStrand` does not apply. This is stated\nrather than proved-nontrivial on purpose: it is the *negation* of a collapse,\nand what it buys is that the `H₃` result must not be quoted for `H₄`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gammaGamma_threeStrand_length_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gammaGamma_threeStrand_length_eq","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L203-L209","doc":"Corollary: a γγ word on three strands has even length `2k`, so the corpus's\neleven-letter nucleon cannot be one — and neither can any word of odd length,\nwhatever its letters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gammaGamma_threeStrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gammaGamma_threeStrand","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L188-L201","doc":"**On three strands there is only one γγ word per length.** A γγ-produced\nword all of whose crossings lie on the two Artin generators of `H₃` is exactly\n`(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)^k`. So the γγ ruling, applied inside `H₃`, leaves a single natural\nnumber of freedom — not a space of orderings, and not a choice of letters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.coreWord_gen_lt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.coreWord_gen_lt_two","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L176-L186","doc":"Every crossing of `coreWord k` lives on generator `0` or `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.coreWord_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.coreWord_length","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L170-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.coreWord_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.coreWord_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L166-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.coreWord_eq_vertexWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.coreWord_eq_vertexWord","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L161-L164","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.coreWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.coreWord","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L155-L159","doc":"`(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)^k`, the only shape a γγ word can take on three strands. `k = 3`\nis `borromean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gammaGamma_index_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gammaGamma_index_lt","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L137-L153","doc":"**On `n` strands there are `n − 2` vertices available**, because `vertex i`\noccupies generators `i` and `i + 1` and the Artin generators are `σ₀ … σ_{n−2}`.\nStated as the bound that is actually used: if every crossing of a γγ word lies\nbelow generator `m`, every vertex index lies below `m − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gammaGamma_iff_vertexWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.gammaGamma_iff_vertexWord","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L119-L135","doc":"**γγ words are exactly the free monoid on the vertices.** The content of\n`GammaGammaWord` is that a word carries an index list and nothing else; the\nstrand count then bounds which indices are available, and every collapse below\nis a corollary of that bound rather than of anything about `H_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.vertexWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.vertexWord","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L113-L117","doc":"The word built from a list of vertex indices: `vertexWord [i, j, k]` is\n`vertex i ++ vertex j ++ vertex k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.altChar_regen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AltCharShiftMultiset.altChar_regen","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AltCharShiftMultiset.lean#L96-L101","doc":"**Re-assigning generators does not move the alternating character.**\n`altChar` reads `Crossing.pos` and never `Crossing.gen`, so any relabelling\n`f : ℕ → ℕ` of the Artin indices leaves it fixed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}